WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:06.372
Nancy knew that she had done the right thing by contacting Rose, but a part of her regretted her actions.

2
00:00:06.373 --> 00:00:10.459
She felt bitter toward Fagin for leading her into a life of crime.

3
00:00:10.460 --> 00:00:14.777
Yet she still didn't want to be the one who brought him within the grasp of the police.

4
00:00:14.778 --> 00:00:23.436
As for Bill Sikes, she had dropped no clues that could lead to his discovery. For his sake she had refused Rose's offers of sanctuary.

5
00:00:23.437 --> 00:00:28.603
She had done all she could for Sikes. She had done the right thing for Oliver.

6
00:00:28.604 --> 00:00:38.119
Although she came to this same conclusion whenever she thought about the situation, Nancy still felt uneasy. She quickly grew pale and thin with anxiety.

7
00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:44.761
It was Sunday night at Bill Sikes' house. Nancy sat silent and dejected with her head in her hands.

8
00:00:44.762 --> 00:00:53.420
When the clock on the nearest church struck the hour, Nancy raised her head, remembering how she'd told Rose to look for her on London Bridge on Sunday nights.

9
00:00:53.421 --> 00:01:04.166
"It's eleven o'clock," said Sikes. He went to the window and peeked through the shutter. "A dark night too. A good night for some illegal business."

10
00:01:04.167 --> 00:01:13.229
"What a pity, Bill, my dear," said Fagin, "that there's none quite ready to be done. We need to plan another robbery now that you're feeling better."

11
00:01:13.230 --> 00:01:17.404
"Yes, we must make up for lost time," said Sikes.

12
00:01:17.405 --> 00:01:25.983
"It does me good to hear you talk like that." Fagin reached over and patted him on the shoulder. "You're quite like yourself again."

13
00:01:25.984 --> 00:01:32.975
They bantered back and forth, ignoring Nancy. Taking advantage of this, she put on her bonnet and started to go out.

14
00:01:32.976 --> 00:01:37.475
But Fagin suddenly noticed her and pulled on Sikes' sleeve.

15
00:01:37.476 --> 00:01:42.951
"Hold on, Nancy!" cried Sikes. "Where are you going at this time of night?"

16
00:01:42.952 --> 00:01:44.858
"Not far."

17
00:01:44.859 --> 00:01:48.991
"What kind of answer is that? Tell me where you're going."

18
00:01:48.992 --> 00:01:51.793
"I don't know where," replied Nancy.

19
00:01:51.793 --> 00:02:01.530
"Then I do. You're going nowhere. Sit down." Sikes said this more out of stubbornness than because he really objected to her going out.

20
00:02:01.531 --> 00:02:06.898
"I'm not well. You know that. I want a breath of air."

21
00:02:06.899 --> 00:02:09.023
"Stick your head out the window."

22
00:02:09.023 --> 00:02:13.768
"I can't get enough air that way. I need to go out on the street."

23
00:02:13.769 --> 00:02:18.601
"You're not going out." Sikes crossed the room and locked the door.

24
00:02:18.602 --> 00:02:22.935
Then he pulled Nancy's bonnet from her head and flung it on top of an old chest.

25
00:02:22.936 --> 00:02:29.998
"Lack of a bonnet won't keep me inside," Nancy said angrily. "Do you know what you're doing, Bill?"

26
00:02:29.999 --> 00:02:37.252
"Know what I'm doing?" Sikes turned to Fagin. "She must be out of her senses or she wouldn't dare talk to me that way."

27
00:02:37.253 --> 00:02:42.903
"You'll drive me to something desperate," Nancy threatened. "Let me go this minute!"

28
00:02:42.904 --> 00:02:45.818
"No!" shouted Sikes.

29
00:02:45.819 --> 00:02:49.245
"Tell him to let me go, Fagin," Nancy said pleadingly.

30
00:02:49.245 --> 00:02:55.070
Fagin continued to watch the scene in silence, wondering why Nancy needed to go out right that minute.

31
00:02:55.071 --> 00:02:59.578
"Bill, you really don't know what you're doing!" Nancy said with great force.

32
00:02:59.579 --> 00:03:05.062
Then she sat down on the floor in front of the door. "Let me go for only an hour."

33
00:03:05.063 --> 00:03:10.475
"I think the girl's gone insane!" said Sikes. "Get up, Nancy."

34
00:03:10.476 --> 00:03:16.895
But Nancy refused to move. Sikes grabbed her and dragged her off to another room.

35
00:03:16.896 --> 00:03:25.300
There he held her captive until the church clock struck midnight and she stopped trying to escape. Leaving her to recover, he returned to Fagin.

36
00:03:25.301 --> 00:03:29.625
"Why do you think she took it into her head to go out tonight?" Bill asked.

37
00:03:29.626 --> 00:03:34.458
Fagin shook his head. "Woman's stubbornness, I suppose, my dear."

38
00:03:34.459 --> 00:03:38.776
As he uttered these words, Nancy reappeared and took her former seat.

39
00:03:38.777 --> 00:03:46.117
"It's time for me to leave," said Fagin. "Could someone bring a light so I don't fall downstairs and break my neck?"

40
00:03:46.118 --> 00:03:49.173
"Show him out, Nancy," said Sikes.

41
00:03:49.174 --> 00:03:57.299
Nancy followed Fagin downstairs with a candle. When they reached the front door, he turned to her and said, "What's the matter, dear?"

42
00:03:57.300 --> 00:03:58.848
"What do you mean?"

43
00:03:58.849 --> 00:04:08.014
Fagin whispered in her ear. "He treats you worse than he treats his dog. If you ever want revenge, come to me."

44
00:04:08.015 --> 00:04:15.585
"Good night," said Nancy without showing any emotion. She shrank back as Fagin tried to pat her hand.

45
00:04:15.586 --> 00:04:19.514
Fagin walked toward home, thinking about what he had just seen.

46
00:04:19.515 --> 00:04:26.911
"Nancy must have fallen in love with someone else," he said to himself. "That's why she's acting so strangely."

47
00:04:26.912 --> 00:04:33.895
He began to think of an evil plot. If he could get Nancy to poison Sikes, that would benefit them both.

48
00:04:33.896 --> 00:04:40.633
She'd no longer be subjected to Sikes' cruelty. He'd no longer have to worry that Sikes might turn against him.

49
00:04:40.634 --> 00:04:49.070
"The man I hate would be gone," Fagin said. "And I'd have unlimited power over Nancy because I'd know that she killed him."

50
00:04:49.071 --> 00:04:59.229
But Nancy might recoil from the idea of killing Sikes. "How can I increase my influence over her?" Fagin wondered as he arrived home.

51
00:04:59.230 --> 00:05:01.964
And suddenly he thought of another plan.

52
00:05:01.965 --> 00:05:05.817
He would send someone to spy on her and catch her with her new love.

53
00:05:05.817 --> 00:05:09.372
Then he could threaten to reveal this information to Sikes.

54
00:05:09.373 --> 00:05:15.364
"She won't be able to refuse my request then." Fagin rubbed his hands together with glee.

55
00:05:15.365 --> 00:05:24.539
The next morning Fagin was up early, waiting for a new member of his gang to appear at the breakfast table. At last the new boy, Bolter, sat down.

56
00:05:24.540 --> 00:05:32.182
Fagin leaned over the table. "Bolter, I want you to do a piece of work for me that requires great care and caution."

57
00:05:32.183 --> 00:05:36.933
"Is it dangerous?" Bolter looked over his cup of coffee.

58
00:05:36.934 --> 00:05:39.953
"No, you only have to follow a young woman."

59
00:05:39.953 --> 00:05:48.674
"I can do that," said the boy. "I was a regular sneak when I was at school. Why am I following her?"

60
00:05:48.675 --> 00:05:54.174
"Just to tell me where she goes, whom she meets, and if possible what she says."

61
00:05:54.175 --> 00:05:56.019
"Who is she?"

62
00:05:56.020 --> 00:06:03.151
"One of us who has gone astray." Fagin got up from the table. "I'll tell you where to find her."

63
00:06:03.151 --> 00:06:11.753
After that Bolter was ready to shadow the woman every day. But it was not until late Sunday night that Fagin finally summoned him to a pub.

64
00:06:11.754 --> 00:06:16.158
"There," whispered Fagin. "Do you see her?"

65
00:06:16.160 --> 00:06:23.398
Bolter nodded. They were hidden behind a small glass panel that enabled them to look down into a room behind the bar.

66
00:06:23.412 --> 00:06:27.303
After a few minutes, the woman got up and left the pub.

67
00:06:27.304 --> 00:06:29.794
"Go!" Fagin nudged Bolter.

68
00:06:29.794 --> 00:06:34.713
"She turned left," said one of Fagin's minions standing at the door to the pub.

69
00:06:34.714 --> 00:06:40.595
Bolter stepped out into the dark street and began to follow Nancy.

